IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mv-act`
IMPORT `mv-third-parties`

-- Motor Vehicles (Third-Party Risks and Compensation) Act 1960, ss 5 to 16
-- -- worked cases.

§ `5 -- agreements with a passenger`

GIVEN `binding` IS A BOOLEAN, `before liability` IS A BOOLEAN, `restricts` IS A BOOLEAN, `volenti` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A PassengerAgreement
DECIDE `a passenger agreement` `binding` `before liability` `restricts` `volenti` IS
    PassengerAgreement WITH
        `section 3 required cover for this use` IS TRUE
        `the person was carried in or upon the vehicle, including entering, getting on to or alighting from it` IS TRUE
        `there was an agreement or understanding between them` IS TRUE
        `it was intended to be legally binding` IS `binding`
        `it was made before the liability arose` IS `before liability`
        `it purports to negative or restrict the liability required to be covered` IS `restricts`
        `it purports to impose conditions on the enforcement of that liability` IS FALSE
        `the person willingly accepted the risk of the user's negligence` IS `volenti`

-- A binding agreement restricting the liability is of no effect.
#ASSERT `the agreement is of no effect under section 5(1)` (`a passenger agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- AND SO IS A NON-BINDING ONE. s 5(1) catches an "agreement or understanding
-- ... whether intended to be legally binding or not", so a mere understanding
-- between driver and passenger is struck down on the same terms.
#ASSERT `the agreement is of no effect under section 5(1)` (`a passenger agreement` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- An agreement made AFTER the liability arose is outside the section.
#ASSERT NOT `the agreement is of no effect under section 5(1)` (`a passenger agreement` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- And one that restricts nothing is untouched.
#ASSERT NOT `the agreement is of no effect under section 5(1)` (`a passenger agreement` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)

-- s 5(2): volenti is excluded outright. Willing acceptance of the risk never
-- negatives the liability, whatever the facts.
#ASSERT NOT `the liability is negatived by the passenger's acceptance of the risk` (`a passenger agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the liability is negatived by the passenger's acceptance of the risk` (`a passenger agreement` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)

§ `7 -- conditions in the policy`

GIVEN `no liability or ceases` IS A BOOLEAN, `after the event` IS A BOOLEAN, `repayment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A PolicyCondition
DECIDE `a policy condition` `no liability or ceases` `after the event` `repayment` IS
    PolicyCondition WITH
        `the condition provides that no liability arises or that liability ceases` IS `no liability or ceases`
        `it operates on something done or omitted AFTER the event giving rise to the claim` IS `after the event`
        `the claim is one mentioned in section 4(1)(b)` IS TRUE
        `the condition requires the insured to repay the insurer sums applied to third party claims` IS `repayment`

-- A condition biting on post-accident conduct -- late notification, say -- is of
-- no effect against the third party.
#ASSERT `the condition is of no effect under section 7(1)` (`a policy condition` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- THE TIMING IS THE WHOLE OF IT. A condition about something to be done BEFORE
-- the accident is untouched, however severe.
#ASSERT NOT `the condition is of no effect under section 7(1)` (`a policy condition` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 7(2): a repayment clause survives, so the insurer pays the victim and
-- recovers from its own insured.
#ASSERT NOT `the condition is of no effect under section 7(1)` (`a policy condition` TRUE TRUE TRUE)

§ `8 -- restrictions on the scope of the policy`

-- Each of the eight listed grounds is struck down.
#ASSERT `the restriction is of no effect under section 8(1)` `the age or physical or mental condition of persons driving the vehicle` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `the restriction is of no effect under section 8(1)` `the condition of the vehicle` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `the restriction is of no effect under section 8(1)` `the times at which or the areas within which the vehicle is used` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `the restriction is of no effect under section 8(1)` `the carrying on the vehicle of any particular apparatus` TRUE TRUE

-- THE LIST IS CLOSED. A restriction by reference to anything not in it stands.
#ASSERT NOT `the restriction is of no effect under section 8(1)` `some ground outside the section 8(1) list` TRUE TRUE

-- The whole section is conditional on a certificate having been issued, as s 9
-- is.
#ASSERT NOT `the restriction is of no effect under section 8(1)` `the condition of the vehicle` FALSE TRUE

-- s 8(3): the insurer recovers from the insured what it paid only because of
-- this section. Same shape as s 7(2).
#ASSERT `the insurer may recover the sum from the insured` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the insurer may recover the sum from the insured` FALSE

§ `10 to 13 -- insolvency`

-- All four s 10(1) events transfer the insured's rights to the third party.
#ASSERT `the insured's rights against the insurer vest in the third party` `the insured became bankrupt or compounded with creditors` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `the insured's rights against the insurer vest in the third party` `a winding up order was made or a voluntary winding up resolution passed` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `the insured's rights against the insurer vest in the third party` `a receiver or manager of the company was duly appointed` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `the insured's rights against the insurer vest in the third party` `a debenture holder took possession under a floating charge` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the insured's rights against the insurer vest in the third party` `no insolvency event` TRUE TRUE

-- "whether BEFORE OR AFTER that event any such liability ... is incurred": the
-- order does not matter, only that the liability was incurred.
#ASSERT NOT `the insured's rights against the insurer vest in the third party` `the insured became bankrupt or compounded with creditors` TRUE FALSE

-- s 12: a dealing after BOTH the liability and the commencement cannot defeat
-- the transferred rights. Both limbs are needed.
#ASSERT `the dealing cannot defeat the third party's rights` (PostTransferDealing WITH `an agreement, waiver, assignment, disposition or payment was made` IS TRUE, `it was made after the liability was incurred` IS TRUE, `it was made after the commencement of the bankruptcy or winding up` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the dealing cannot defeat the third party's rights` (PostTransferDealing WITH `an agreement, waiver, assignment, disposition or payment was made` IS TRUE, `it was made after the liability was incurred` IS TRUE, `it was made after the commencement of the bankruptcy or winding up` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the dealing cannot defeat the third party's rights` (PostTransferDealing WITH `an agreement, waiver, assignment, disposition or payment was made` IS TRUE, `it was made after the liability was incurred` IS FALSE, `it was made after the commencement of the bankruptcy or winding up` IS TRUE)

-- s 13(1): the liability itself survives the insolvency, so the third party
-- keeps both routes -- against the insurer and against the insured.
#ASSERT `the liability survives the insolvency event` `the insured became bankrupt or compounded with creditors` TRUE

§ `11 -- the duty to say whether there was a policy`

GIVEN `insured` IS A BOOLEAN, `would have been` IS A BOOLEAN, `stated` IS A BOOLEAN, `particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN InformationDemand
DECIDE `a demand where` `insured` `would have been` `stated` `particulars` IS
    InformationDemand WITH
        `a claim was made in respect of a liability required to be covered by section 4(1)(b)` IS TRUE
        `a demand was made by or on behalf of the claimant` IS TRUE
        `the person was insured in respect of that liability` IS `insured`
        `the person would have been insured had the insurer not avoided or cancelled the policy` IS `would have been`
        `the person stated whether or not they were insured` IS `stated`
        `the person gave the particulars specified in the certificate` IS `particulars`

#ASSERT NOT `the person has contravened section 11(1)` (`a demand where` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the person has contravened section 11(1)` (`a demand where` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- THE SECOND LIMB. A driver whose policy the insurer has AVOIDED must still
-- disclose it and give the certificate particulars -- otherwise the s 9 route,
-- which survives avoidance, could never be found by the claimant.
#ASSERT `particulars are owed as well as a statement` (`a demand where` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the person has contravened section 11(1)` (`a demand where` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person has contravened section 11(1)` (`a demand where` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)

-- Someone who never was and never would have been insured owes the statement
-- and no particulars.
#ASSERT NOT `particulars are owed as well as a statement` (`a demand where` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person has contravened section 11(1)` (`a demand where` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)

§ `14 -- settlements`

-- "any claim which MIGHT be made": the protection reaches a claim not yet
-- brought, so the insurer cannot buy off the insured before the victim sues.
#ASSERT `the settlement is invalid under section 14(1)` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the settlement is invalid under section 14(1)` TRUE TRUE

-- s 14(2): the policy survives the insured's death, "as if the insured person
-- were still alive".
#ASSERT `the policy remains available to third parties` TRUE
#ASSERT `the policy remains available to third parties` FALSE

§ `15 -- the 7 day surrender, which decides whether the victim is paid`

GIVEN `cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN, `done` IS A BOOLEAN, `days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A SurrenderFacts
DECIDE `surrender facts` `cancelled` `done` `days` IS
    SurrenderFacts WITH
        `a certificate of insurance was issued under section 4(9)` IS TRUE
        `the policy was cancelled by mutual consent or under the policy` IS `cancelled`
        `the certificate was surrendered or a statutory declaration of loss made` IS `done`
        `days from the taking effect of the cancellation when that was done` IS `days`

#ASSERT NOT `the person has contravened section 15(1)` (`surrender facts` TRUE TRUE 7)
#ASSERT `the person has contravened section 15(1)` (`surrender facts` TRUE TRUE 8)
#ASSERT `the person has contravened section 15(1)` (`surrender facts` TRUE FALSE 0)
-- No cancellation, no duty.
#ASSERT NOT `the person has contravened section 15(1)` (`surrender facts` FALSE FALSE 0)

-- s 15(2) and s 16(2): the escalating penalty.
#ASSERT `the maximum fine in dollars` FALSE EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `the maximum fine in dollars` TRUE EQUALS 1000

§ `16 -- production of the certificate`

GIVEN `own name` IS A BOOLEAN, `owner name` IS A BOOLEAN, `certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A ProductionDemand
DECIDE `a production demand` `own name` `owner name` `certificate` IS
    ProductionDemand WITH
        `the person was driving a motor vehicle on a road` IS TRUE
        `a police officer required it` IS TRUE
        `the person gave their own name and address` IS `own name`
        `the person gave the owner's name and address` IS `owner name`
        `the person produced the certificate` IS `certificate`

#ASSERT NOT `the person has contravened section 16(1)` (`a production demand` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- Any one of the three omissions is the contravention.
#ASSERT `the person has contravened section 16(1)` (`a production demand` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the person has contravened section 16(1)` (`a production demand` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the person has contravened section 16(1)` (`a production demand` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
